<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haute-Savoie</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haute-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savoie">Savoie</a> is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, with Annecy as its prefecture. It covers the northern part of the former Duchy of Savoy, including the Chablais, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-of-geneva">Genevois</a> and the Mont Blanc massif. It was created in 1860 when Savoy was ceded to France by the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haute-savoie.jpg" alt="Haute-Savoie" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tiia Monto · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Les_Houches_view_2_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
